---
description: Workflow rules for using Cursor skills, subagents, MCPs and iterative design prototypes.
alwaysApply: true
---
- Use skills for repeatable multi-step workflows and subagents for context-isolated specialist work.
- For large visual tasks, delegate browser inspection or independent visual critique rather than stuffing all evidence into the parent context.
- Before adding a dependency, inspect whether Next.js, React, Motion, Tailwind or shadcn already solves the requirement.
- Use the shadcn MCP for component discovery rather than blindly generating primitives.
- Use Playwright for browser verification and screenshot-based checks.
- When the task requests a new visual direction, produce competing prototypes before consolidating them.
- Do not declare a design complete based only on source-code inspection.
